Excellent! All three starting materials are commercially available. The route is:

**Summary:**
- **Step 1**: Reductive amination of 3-fluoroazetidine-1-carbaldehyde (O=CN1CC(F)C1) with 4-(chloromethyl)benzaldehyde (O=Cc1ccc(CCl)cc1) to form FC1CN(Cc2ccc(CCl)cc2)C1
- **Step 2**: N-alkylation of the triazole amide (COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1) with the benzyl chloride intermediate to form the target molecule

The route has 2 steps (well under the 3-step limit) and the total cost is approximately $1,734 (well under the $9,999 budget).

